WEBVTT

00:06.170 --> 00:07.580
It's pitch black in here...

00:09.670 --> 00:11.000
And it's flooded.

00:28.420 --> 00:29.380
It's trying...

00:29.880 --> 00:31.420
...to crush my eyeballs!

00:46.500 --> 00:47.580
Her eyeballs...

00:48.420 --> 00:49.710
...they're gone!

00:50.000 --> 00:53.420
Where? Where? Where?!

00:53.420 --> 00:55.830
Where are they? Where?!

01:08.830 --> 01:09.790
Stop!

01:11.000 --> 01:13.250
I'll look! I'll find them!

01:14.210 --> 01:16.710
Please stop hurting me!

01:17.080 --> 01:20.330
Where are you? Take my place!

01:21.080 --> 01:22.830
He wants us to play tag.

01:22.960 --> 01:23.710
What?

01:24.290 --> 01:27.040
If he catches us, then that's the fate awaiting us.

01:27.630 --> 01:29.630
That's what he's trying to communicate.

01:30.330 --> 01:32.130
The only rule is "don't get caught."

01:32.460 --> 01:36.040
So, we win if we save Eiko and escape the tunnel.

01:37.210 --> 01:39.790
Though, it doesn't look like he wants us to win.

01:40.080 --> 01:42.460
He wants to watch us struggle and fail.

01:44.250 --> 01:46.960
It moves slow. Let's get this over with quickly.

03:25.750 --> 03:27.170
I'll keep him occupied.

03:27.540 --> 03:32.210
Eiko might not be able to walk out on her own,
and I won't be able to carry her.

03:32.830 --> 03:34.170
That'll be up to you.

03:38.210 --> 03:38.960
Got it!

03:43.210 --> 03:44.330
...-kun...

03:44.580 --> 03:47.630
Kei-kun... Kei-kun...

03:53.500 --> 03:54.420
Eiko!

03:57.040 --> 03:58.580
She's gagged, though...

03:59.250 --> 04:01.580
So, who was calling for me?

04:02.830 --> 04:04.790
Kei-kun...

04:06.000 --> 04:16.540
Kei-kun... Kei-kun... Kei-kun... Kei-kun...

04:23.580 --> 04:26.130
Without this doll, I'd be dead meat!

04:28.000 --> 04:28.790
Can you walk?

04:29.380 --> 04:31.750
No, I hurt my leg...

04:34.130 --> 04:36.920
Eiko, can you hold the light and the doll?

04:37.790 --> 04:39.710
Thanks. Sorry about this.

04:40.380 --> 04:43.830
Now our problem is how to get past that spirit.

04:44.830 --> 04:45.710
Wait, it's gone?!

04:47.420 --> 04:48.130
Run!

04:56.040 --> 04:58.130
Th-that was close!

04:58.670 --> 05:00.670
We're out of dolls to take hits for us.

05:01.210 --> 05:05.080
Without those, we'll take damage from whatever hits us.

05:05.580 --> 05:06.750
Back me up.

05:07.290 --> 05:07.960
Okay!

05:08.460 --> 05:11.250
Coming is easy.

05:11.500 --> 05:13.580
Going is scary.

05:45.540 --> 05:46.710
Keep running!

05:53.000 --> 05:54.290
Almost there!

05:58.290 --> 05:59.710
Caught you!

05:59.880 --> 06:02.330
You're gonna go straight to Hell!

06:12.920 --> 06:13.710
We're out!

06:35.420 --> 06:36.330
Yayoi-chan!

06:36.790 --> 06:37.710
Are you okay?!

06:37.880 --> 06:39.080
Only thanks to you, Eiko.

06:39.580 --> 06:42.210
We all got out of the tunnel safe and sound.

06:42.830 --> 06:43.630
Now...

07:03.460 --> 07:05.880
I'm just as ready to fight you, too.

07:06.210 --> 07:08.710
Everything's in place to unleash my Graduate.

07:09.960 --> 07:12.040
The High Priest's curse comes on slow and steady.

07:12.460 --> 07:15.040
It doesn't work well against enemies
who are trying to kill you quickly.

07:16.000 --> 07:18.290
This Graduate will work much better.

07:19.460 --> 07:20.630
Stand back a little more.

07:20.960 --> 07:21.540
Huh?

07:22.500 --> 07:23.380
You don't wanna get caught in this.

07:28.130 --> 07:31.630
I feel it... The Graduate!

07:37.420 --> 07:38.540
Revel in a heroic death...

07:57.540 --> 07:59.750
...Imprisoned Martyr.

08:10.710 --> 08:14.290
About six months ago, I happened across him.

08:14.960 --> 08:20.130
From what I heard, he returned to Japan
after the war and lived a long life.

08:20.630 --> 08:24.880
But after death, for some reason,
he returned to his wartime self.

08:25.790 --> 08:31.380
Then, the spirits of enemy soldiers clinging to him
began devouring the ghosts in nearby graves.

08:32.540 --> 08:37.420
Unable to pass on to the afterlife, and grieving
for the suffering he brought to those around him,

08:37.750 --> 08:40.040
he had but one desperate wish:

08:41.000 --> 08:42.420
Kill me.

08:43.170 --> 08:46.380
The soldier so fierce he was called
"immortal" on the battlefield,

08:46.710 --> 08:50.830
trapped in a cruel prison,
fated to die for his country over and over again...

08:51.500 --> 08:55.000
Nicknamed, The Imprisoned Martyr.

08:53.580 --> 08:56.460
<b>THE IMPRISONED MARTYR</b>

09:37.790 --> 09:40.040
Just try to carve off my face.

09:47.880 --> 09:49.290
Kill me.

10:02.040 --> 10:04.170
It got weaker? How?!

10:05.330 --> 10:06.290
Is it his curse?

10:06.630 --> 10:11.960
The Martyr isn't an evil spirit,
so it's less of a curse, and more of a prayer.

10:12.670 --> 10:16.500
Anyone within the lines on the ground
feels his emotions and will.

10:16.830 --> 10:22.420
The wounds he suffered in the war,
his starvation, fatigue, insomnia...

10:23.000 --> 10:27.670
The torment of being unable to die,
no matter your anguish.

10:28.630 --> 10:32.790
It makes them feel so weak and hopeless
that they're begging to be killed.

10:33.380 --> 10:35.880
That is what the Martyr does to his victims.

10:36.580 --> 10:42.130
There's only one way
to escape his torment: kill the Martyr.

10:43.380 --> 10:50.630
While the spirit is still weak, it must break through
the Martyr's defenses, and destroy his immortal body.

10:53.750 --> 10:56.630
Eiko, I'm gonna video call you, so pick up.

10:57.630 --> 10:58.290
Okay.

11:00.080 --> 11:03.630
We can use this to keep an eye on things
from a safe distance.

11:04.210 --> 11:05.420
How does that work?

11:06.000 --> 11:09.500
With every new weapon the Martyr draws,

11:09.750 --> 11:13.580
his Weakening Prayer progresses
to the next of three stages and gets even bigger.

11:13.830 --> 11:17.790
If we get caught in it, we need to end things
while it's still in its second stage.

11:18.000 --> 11:23.920
If it gets to the third stage, we'll all be suffocated
and paralyzed, and we won't be able to die.

11:24.290 --> 11:28.210
Worst case scenario, we'd have to endure
burtal agony for a century or more.

11:29.710 --> 11:31.580
The pattern on the ground expands pretty quick.

11:31.710 --> 11:33.790
We need to get some distance while we still can.

11:36.750 --> 11:38.130
If you want it to stop...

11:43.210 --> 11:44.540
...then kill me.

12:22.040 --> 12:23.790
I can't die.

12:24.540 --> 12:26.460
I'm still too strong.

12:27.710 --> 12:30.080
Perhaps if I were weaker...

12:32.210 --> 12:33.580
you could kill me.

12:39.460 --> 12:40.170
What?!

12:40.540 --> 12:42.330
It's moved into the second stage.

12:43.000 --> 12:45.420
We really want it to finish it off here.

12:52.420 --> 12:53.580
Come on.

12:55.000 --> 12:57.250
Kill me.

14:09.210 --> 14:11.960
I'm still not dead.

14:13.250 --> 14:15.750
But that's all right.

14:16.500 --> 14:20.290
Once more. I'll weaken myself once more.

14:20.790 --> 14:22.380
Please kill me.

14:25.290 --> 14:28.290
Keitaro, we should be good here! Hurry!

14:31.880 --> 14:33.290
Sorry, Eiko!

14:41.960 --> 14:43.420
No, his feet!

14:43.710 --> 14:44.380
Eiko!

14:44.880 --> 14:45.670
On it!

14:51.000 --> 14:52.000
Thanks...

15:19.750 --> 15:21.580
I don't want to die.

15:25.710 --> 15:28.580
I don't want to die.

15:34.670 --> 15:36.290
I need water.

16:02.210 --> 16:02.790
Ki...

16:03.880 --> 16:05.540
Kill... me...

16:11.960 --> 16:13.540
We go together.

16:29.080 --> 16:30.330
If not today...

16:30.670 --> 16:35.580
...then one day, will someone please kill me?

16:44.460 --> 16:45.290
It's over.

16:46.830 --> 16:47.580
Let's head back.

16:57.040 --> 17:01.130
Do you want to get eaten, or live on? You pick.

17:04.790 --> 17:09.290
Yayoi-chan, are you sure
you should be capturing a ghost this evil...?

17:09.500 --> 17:12.380
I told you I'd do anything to win, be it good or evil.

17:13.750 --> 17:16.880
I'll take a man-eating fiend if I can use it.

17:23.380 --> 17:30.130
If I come with you... will I be able to kill more?

17:30.960 --> 17:32.420
Yes, but you'll rest first.

17:33.790 --> 17:36.170
Then I'll live on.

17:36.790 --> 17:37.710
My thanks.

17:44.830 --> 17:47.880
WHAT HAVE YOU DONE TO ME?!

17:48.080 --> 17:51.380
When spirits possess something,
they conform to its physical state.

17:51.830 --> 17:56.880
I'm going to make you experience
the pain and suffering you inflicted on your victims.

17:57.040 --> 17:59.210
YOU LITTLE BRAT! LET ME OUT!

17:59.210 --> 18:04.040
I NEED TO KILL, KILL, KILL, KILL!

18:04.420 --> 18:07.880
You'll never feel that thrill ever again.

18:08.380 --> 18:10.580
I'll liberate you from your murderous urges.

18:14.290 --> 18:16.170
Keep your head empty.

18:16.460 --> 18:21.080
Your wasted tenacity
will make you a fine proxy protector.

18:21.790 --> 18:27.790
She captured it, sealed its evil urges,
then forced it to suffer, all in one fell swoop...

18:29.080 --> 18:32.670
Got me the spirit of the Old Old F Tunnel.

18:34.750 --> 18:37.420
Keitaro, Eiko, wait here for a sec.

18:37.790 --> 18:38.380
Huh?

18:40.920 --> 18:44.380
<b>minutes</b>

18:40.920 --> 18:44.380
<b>later...</b>

18:44.790 --> 18:47.130
Yayoi-chan, what're you doing?

18:47.290 --> 18:48.080
Cleaning up.

18:48.540 --> 18:50.710
These go to a temple. These go to my room.

18:50.920 --> 18:51.880
What's that mean?

18:52.830 --> 18:57.000
I gathered up the spirits of the Old Old F Tunnel's victims.

18:57.380 --> 18:58.880
Then, I sorted them into three groups:

18:58.880 --> 19:05.630
Pure victims, victims in tough situations,
and victims who joined him and went evil.

19:06.380 --> 19:07.420
How'd you do that?

19:08.000 --> 19:08.830
Easy.

19:09.790 --> 19:15.460
The Martyr's prayer weakened all the victim spirits,
so I asked them one question.

19:16.500 --> 19:19.130
Want me to take you over to another spirit?

19:19.750 --> 19:27.500
Those who said "I don't get it," or refused because
they didn't want to kill someone else, are all good spirits.

19:28.130 --> 19:29.170
On the other hand,

19:29.630 --> 19:31.330
HURRY THE FUCK UP!

19:31.420 --> 19:36.250
Spirits who knew eating another spirit
would make them stronger, and still wanted it,

19:36.250 --> 19:39.580
would totally be okay with sacrificing someone else
for their own selfish needs.

19:39.830 --> 19:42.170
Which means they probably already did.

19:43.080 --> 19:48.290
So, I asked every spirit
"Did someone take you down with them?"

19:48.790 --> 19:52.920
After getting those answers, I knew who was
temple-bound and who was a baddie.

19:54.330 --> 19:56.330
The baddies are headed to my room.

19:58.380 --> 19:59.540
What happened to Anna?

20:00.920 --> 20:01.710
Let's go.

20:03.540 --> 20:06.500
Thanks, guys, for helping out.

20:06.750 --> 20:08.040
Don't worry about it.

20:08.330 --> 20:11.710
Eiko, are you good to drive?

20:11.710 --> 20:12.960
Yeah, I'm fine!

20:13.880 --> 20:18.670
I've done nothing but muck things up
for you this time, so I gotta pull my weight!

20:19.000 --> 20:22.170
You helped out plenty tonight. Right?

20:22.170 --> 20:22.880
Yeah.

20:24.080 --> 20:25.210
Thanks.

20:28.040 --> 20:28.500
Huh?!

20:28.750 --> 20:29.580
Eiko?

20:29.830 --> 20:30.790
What's wrong?

20:31.170 --> 20:34.750
I-I didn't even press the button...

20:35.580 --> 20:36.500
So why...?

20:39.630 --> 20:41.040
It's not fair!

20:41.500 --> 20:46.460
I went through all that pain, but you get to leave alive?!

20:46.460 --> 20:48.170
It's not fair!

20:48.170 --> 20:50.040
You're gonna stay here, too!

20:50.040 --> 20:53.630
SUFFER AND DIE!

21:05.540 --> 21:06.750
She still had all her strength.

21:06.960 --> 21:09.380
Has she been clinging to Eiko this whole time?

21:09.830 --> 21:10.710
That's on me.

21:10.920 --> 21:14.250
But don't think you get to rest in peace
after those stunts you pull-

21:14.250 --> 21:15.000
Wait!

21:16.330 --> 21:21.750
For a little while, we were almost friends...

21:29.040 --> 21:31.250
Then I'll let you decide how to handle her.

21:36.040 --> 21:38.880
Sorry... and thank you.

21:39.710 --> 21:42.750
And so, with the help of our Graduate,

21:43.170 --> 21:49.380
we successfully concluded our investigation
of the S-Rank spirit in the F Tunnel.

23:21.960 --> 23:27.040
After barely escaping the tunnel with her life,
Eiko struggles with her lingering fear.

23:28.000 --> 23:32.330
Will she truly be able to help
Yayoi and Keitaro on their next mission?

23:33.420 --> 23:39.670
To steel her resolve, Eiko sets out
to one of the most haunted spots in Kanto.
